{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror","id":998322,"title":"Chronicles of Darkness not as horror","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T11:11:00-07:00","id":998322,"title":"Chronicles of Darkness not as horror","content":"I do not play Chronicles of Darkness because they are horror games. Horror scares me, and I don't like that. I play them because you can play a vampire or a mage or a hunter, and that makes me feel empowered. I play CoD for the angst (I love angst), for the romance, for the intrigue and scheming, but NOT for the horror. Am I alone in this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:28:21-07:00","id":998334,"title":"","content":"It's not really the centerpoint of my games but it is definitely there. I think that you lose something if you focus overabundantly on a single aspect. You need angst, romance, intrigue, scheming but also horror, tragedy and even things like hope and (for me at least) comedy.<br /> <br /> All in all as a storyteller you have to make your game entertaining, use whatever means at your disposition to make that happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But i think there is a perception of conflict when the game is presented as a horror game. Horror is there most assuredly but i dont think its meant to be the only flavor of the Chronicles of Darkness. All the same becoming a vampire is not meant to be considered a purely positive outcome either.<br /> <br /> Hope i have communicated my thoughts clearly. I tend to ramble and have a difficulty translating thoughts to words. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:33:40-07:00","id":998384,"title":"","content":"CofD is a game system with many splats, each of which are adaptable enough to wear many masks. Horror is just one flavour of many.<br /> <br /> Me, personally, I like horror, but it is very much a sometimes food. If a game is an unrelenting march of horror, people break under it. That can be fun, now and then, as catharsis, but do it all the time and it gets dull.<br /> <br /> I've had one Mage game include stories of horror and betrayal - with generational sins, questions of temptation to use awful means to achieve terrible ends, and cultish altars slicked with gore and tears - but this game has also had stories of love, heroism, and moments of downright childish wonder (the most recent being a father sitting with his daughter and teaching her with breathless awe the names of the real, living, breathing dinosaurs wandering by in front of them).<br /> <br /> Make your stories what's fun for you and your friends. If you look hard enough, you'll find people just as in love with your style of stories as you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:49:12-07:00","id":998395,"title":"","content":"I've made me case adamantly enough elsewhere. Folks who come at these games and drop half of the premise will never make any sense to me (the Dresden Files RPG is right there, and so are Monsterhearts and Urban Shadows!) but at least you're having fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:51:52-07:00","id":998396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=998395#post998395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made me case adamantly enough elsewhere. Folks who come at these games and drop half of the premise will never make any sense to me (the Dresden Files RPG is right there, and so are Monsterhearts and Urban Shadows!) but at least you're having fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could just be a ruleset thing, and affection for some of the lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:54:03-07:00","id":998398,"title":"","content":"You're not alone, there's plenty of people who do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T13:00:48-07:00","id":998402,"title":"","content":"Hm. Well, I tend to come at them as horror games first and foremost, but horror is an especially hard genre to keep balanced in long form narrative, so it's typically not the <i>only</i> genre element in the game.How much of a role it plays comes down to the style of my players and the type of setting we're working with, but I think horror is too baked into the mechanics to excise it completely without hurting the game.<br /> <br /> So my Hunter the game has a tone of action-comedy modeled off 80s pop culture pastiches, but that makes it easy to blindside my characters with those rare and raw moments where they realize the horror of what they're up against. My take on Requiem is largely political, but it grinds the characters down into a routine of increasingly morally dubious actions until they take a step back and see what their characters have become. And my Changeling... Actually Changeling is just horrifying all around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 11-04-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T13:27:12-07:00","id":998414,"title":"","content":"You're not alone. Plenty of people aren't interested in the horror aspect, and that's fine. This is a hobby we do for fun, so if you have more fun de-emphasizing the horror and focusing on other aspects of the game, there is absolutely nothing wrong with that. I do think you'll probably find yourself fighting against the system at times to accomplish that aim, but if that extra effort is worthwhile to you, then have at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:05:14-07:00","id":998457,"title":"","content":"I don't think myself that you need to fight against the system to get rid of horror. The very same rules who work for horror in CoD also works for other kinds of drama.<br /> <br /> By myself, I like to vary. Sometimes horror is my meat and bread. Sometimes I just use the spooky themes that I love to focus on the same genres cited by the OP, and even others. I did comedy with it (we have a word for comedy-horror pastiche here in Brazil, its called &quot;Terrir&quot; (Teh-Reer)), a lot. Right now my vibe is more on the focus on the weirdness, not necessarily the horror of it.<br /> <br /> Even then, I always give credit to the idea of looking out for other games. I understand and agree with keeping with CoD for your game, but I also tried the aforementioned Monsterhearts and it was simply fantastic for some games. I'm also going to make an experiment with the setting on the Mutants and Masterminds 2nd Edition System.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:07:52-07:00","id":998460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror#post998322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not play Chronicles of Darkness because they are horror games. Horror scares me, and I don't like that. I play them because you can play a vampire or a mage or a hunter, and that makes me feel empowered. I play CoD for the angst (I love angst), for the romance, for the intrigue and scheming, but NOT for the horror. Am I alone in this?</div> </div> </div> </div> Mirrors rules on removing the mortality checks from the game would be useful for producing a feeling of angst as would promethean (both versions), &amp; vampire and werewolf both have some good ideas for romantic games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:46:41-07:00","id":998476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=998457#post998457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think myself that you need to fight against the system to get rid of horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> RPGs can never automatically be scary since horror, just like humour, is all in the delivery. If you don't roleplay it as a horror game it really isn't. Power fantasy and/or drama is just as viable without changing anything in the written material. Not that they're mutually exclusive with horror.<br /> (That said, what makes CofD a good horror game instead of just an urban fantasy RPG is how easy it is to play as a horror game.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T16:06:48-07:00","id":998486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=998395#post998395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (the Dresden Files RPG is right there, and so are Monsterhearts and Urban Shadows!) but at least you're having fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in my case, Dresden Files is FATE which i think is a bad system, urban Shadows and Monster hearts is Apocalypse world which i dont like for campaigns so not much to do than use WoD.<br /> <br /> Now if the people doing FFG SW or Shadowrun would release a supernatural copy-paste game.....<br /> <br /> Personally i dont like horror, i think some aspect of it is loss after the 7th dick joke on the table but i have seen good stuff written in PbP games.<br /> <br /> I prefer the complex politics and cool powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T16:10:47-07:00","id":998488,"title":"","content":"Personally i use mirrors to do no mortality stat + deal-making magic as an intensely philosophical urban fantasy chronicle but that's probably a harder pitch than &quot;intense supernatural drama&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T16:35:32-07:00","id":998495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=998486#post998486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i dont like horror, i think some aspect of it is loss after the 7th dick joke on the table but i have seen good stuff written in PbP games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think the best horror doesn't shy away from humor. The best horror knows it can be funny and still be scary. Look at anything by Wes Craven.<br /> <br /> That said, horror definitely does require player buy-in, and if your players don't want to treat the game as horror, it won't be. So I do get what you mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T16:49:32-07:00","id":998502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=998486#post998486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well in my case, Dresden Files is FATE which i think is a bad system, urban Shadows and Monster hearts is Apocalypse world which i dont like for campaigns so not much to do than use WoD.<br /> <br /> Now if the people doing FFG SW or Shadowrun would release a supernatural copy-paste game.....<br /> <br /> Personally i dont like horror, i think some aspect of it is loss after the 7th dick joke on the table but i have seen good stuff written in PbP games.<br /> <br /> I prefer the complex politics and cool powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but laugh at someone who calls FATE a bad system and then ask for Shadowrun in the same breath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T17:10:17-07:00","id":998507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=998502#post998502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't help but laugh at someone who calls FATE a bad system and then ask for Shadowrun in the same breath.</div> </div> </div> </div>FATE is like an empty beer bootle that people said is the best beer in the world because someone could, potentially, fill it with said beer.<br /> <br /> Is the barebones of a system that ask of the player groups to fill in as game dev for it and lives or dies by the buy-in/skill of said group more than any merit of the system itself. <br /> <br /> FATE only merit is being not obtrusive.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun 5th on the other hand is a robust but functional system with the only sin of a parent company that completely screw the devs. Causing to rush constantly the books and delay the erratas to fix it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-04-2016, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T17:19:46-07:00","id":998510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=998395#post998395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made me case adamantly enough elsewhere. Folks who come at these games and drop half of the premise will never make any sense to me (the Dresden Files RPG is right there, and so are Monsterhearts and Urban Shadows!) but at least you're having fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every single part of an RPG is an advisory note. Some system handle things better than others and it can be useful to skin the beast and drape it in fresh leather instead of trying to make a new animal altogether. Chronicles of Darkness provides a diverse range of ways to play it, and it's entirely possible to turn the game into a very wide array of play styles. The base game can have all the supernatural elements excised and be played as a strict investigation story, for example, with nothing lost.<br /> <br /> Personally, I love the setting as-is, but that doesn't mean I've not meticulously picked it apart like a dice-loving discount Jeremy Bentham. I've used the bones of CofD and its splats to make at least two entire fantasy settings, for example. I'm on my way to using Exalted 3e to make a third.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T22:53:28-07:00","id":998627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=998395#post998395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made me case adamantly enough elsewhere. Folks who come at these games and drop half of the premise will never make any sense to me (the Dresden Files RPG is right there, and so are Monsterhearts and Urban Shadows!) but at least you're having fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>As has been noted, rule set is a big thing. Yes, there might be other systems made for running the type of game someone is wanting to run, but just because they were made for that purpose doesn't make them good (be it objectively or just by the sensibilities of the person wanting to run said game). The solution a lot of people come to is to find the system they like the most that fits the closest/easiest to what they want and to then jury rig that. There's a reason there's a d20 version of pretty much everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T00:50:20-07:00","id":998641,"title":"","content":"I think that <b>CoD</b> games are best described as dark urban fantasy, with 'mortals' take as most horror-ish. Each gameline have elements both really in horror area, but also those as more urban fantasy and playing those can get you different 'flavors' of CoD games or even different chronicles in the same game.<br /> <br /> Vampire has both Beast and Banes ( clearly horror tropes ) but also Disciplines ( one for more fantasy ) and some mixed bags ( like Blood Bonds ). Mages are much more on fantasy scale ( magic, yay! ) but also have some very horror elements still ( Abyss, Paradox, Obsessions, Ephemera &amp; Intruders ). Changeling is probably the highest in fantasy, but still delivers horror elements ( like every scary antagonists send by True Fae or Lords and Ladies themselves ).<br /> <br /> What is ratio of fantasy to horror on your table depends on chosen game, particular chronicle foundations and general this parties tastest. And probably many other things also...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T00:50:48-07:00","id":998642,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I don't use CofD for horror, specifically. What I've been saying recently is that CofD is that it's really, really good for introspective play, horror or not, because so much of the props and tools available are intended as triggers for making opportunities to introspect. And horror is a <i>really</i> good way to narrow a designer's focus down in a way that supports introspective play really well, even if the players aren't using it that way.<br /> <br /> I know that that's not how most people use it, but that's what I like about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T04:37:16-07:00","id":998697,"title":"","content":"I never really used CoD as a horror setting. Mystery, conspiracy, and paranormal sure, but horror is only a by-product of whatever is going on compared to the main driving genre. So now, you're not alone in not setting your CoD sessions as non-horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T04:51:53-07:00","id":998700,"title":"","content":"My style of running CofD is more urban-fantasy than horror. Urban-Fantasy in a dark world, but the real world is pretty dark already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:36:01-07:00","id":998753,"title":"","content":"Why are some people fighting about &quot;My System Is Bettah&quot; here? Well, lets at least do it in a more constructive manner...<br /> <br /> I played and liked Monsterhearts. The catch of the system is to focus on relations than anything else. Like, every aspect of the system is about relations and how to play them, use them, and abuse them, both as means and end. It is good when your mainly concern in the chronicle is the soup opera aspect. Very good, indeed, even for long term chronicles.<br /> <br /> My only experience with FATE is Accelerated. I liked it pretty much, and it is good when you need to focus on fast and creative action of any type. It is really good at being easy to apply any kind of solution you can think of, to any given problem. It is also good for crossovers where you want to guarantee balance without loosing the characteristics of any given character.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun 5th Ed I didn't read yet, I kind of forgot it... its a shame, since I'm a big fan of 2nd Ed, even it being such a messy system. What I can say about 2nd Ed is that it delivers lethality. The major problem of it is to make money into a category you must choose how much to focus on character creation.<br /> <br /> D20 already have Mont Cook's World of Darkness. It is very interesting, if very distinct. I also adapted some cWoD splats myself to TRPG, a brazilian d20, for a chronicle I was playing. It also made some interesting ways of playing WoD. The focus on balanced levels makes for an interesting way of play.<br /> <br /> CoD, in the same way, have a lot of particular characteristics and tools that make it for a distinct behavior as system. That's not only a reason to play it with other genres. I actually specifically choose CoD system for both my adaptations on Pok\u00e9mon and Green Lantern Corps for the characteristics of the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T10:52:36-07:00","id":998818,"title":"","content":"Maitrecorbo: Thank you. Your post was especially helpful. Here's the thing: I find that being able to play the monster (whether a vampire, werewolf or whatever) makes that creature a lot less frightening. Also, breaking it down, analyzing it and, most importantly, understanding it (as I try to do in my World of Darkness timeline) gets rid of a lot of the horror that comes from the monster being unknown and frightening. Put it this way: I could never watch The Exorcist. Maybe I'm being silly, but that's just me. Anyway, thanks to all you guys who posted. I really appreciate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:01:30-07:00","id":998824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=998753#post998753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are some people fighting about &quot;My System Is Bettah&quot; here? Well, lets at least do it in a more constructive manner...<br /> <br /> I played and liked Monsterhearts. The catch of the system is to focus on relations than anything else. Like, every aspect of the system is about relations and how to play them, use them, and abuse them, both as means and end. It is good when your mainly concern in the chronicle is the soup opera aspect. Very good, indeed, even for long term chronicles.<br /> <br /> My only experience with FATE is Accelerated. I liked it pretty much, and it is good when you need to focus on fast and creative action of any type. It is really good at being easy to apply any kind of solution you can think of, to any given problem. It is also good for crossovers where you want to guarantee balance without loosing the characteristics of any given character.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun 5th Ed I didn't read yet, I kind of forgot it... its a shame, since I'm a big fan of 2nd Ed, even it being such a messy system. What I can say about 2nd Ed is that it delivers lethality. The major problem of it is to make money into a category you must choose how much to focus on character creation.<br /> <br /> D20 already have Mont Cook's World of Darkness. It is very interesting, if very distinct. I also adapted some cWoD splats myself to TRPG, a brazilian d20, for a chronicle I was playing. It also made some interesting ways of playing WoD. The focus on balanced levels makes for an interesting way of play.<br /> <br /> CoD, in the same way, have a lot of particular characteristics and tools that make it for a distinct behavior as system. That's not only a reason to play it with other genres. I actually specifically choose CoD system for both my adaptations on Pok\u00e9mon and Green Lantern Corps for the characteristics of the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont forget GURPS WOD. I heard their mage version is quite good but i have being able to get around reading it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:03:31-08:00","id":999216,"title":"","content":"Never get much opportunity on GURPS books, though I heard about GURPS WOD. But a book of GURPS that I did got was GURPS Illuminatti, and I simply don't have words to say how good it is, and how much I actually use it on WoD and CoD. If anyone likes to use the conspiracy take, in whatever scale, I highly recommend the read of GURPS Illuminatti.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:15:09-08:00","id":999221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=999216#post999216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never get much opportunity on GURPS books, though I heard about GURPS WOD. But a book of GURPS that I did got was GURPS Illuminatti, and I simply don't have words to say how good it is, and how much I actually use it on WoD and CoD. If anyone likes to use the conspiracy take, in whatever scale, I highly recommend the read of GURPS Illuminatti.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it have any info on how to RP a conspiracy/cult of that nature? I am looking info about that for a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:12:40-08:00","id":999252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998322-chronicles-of-darkness-not-as-horror?p=999221#post999221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it have any info on how to RP a conspiracy/cult of that nature? I am looking info about that for a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even being a reasonably big book, there is almost no rules on it. GURPS Illuminatti is by far mostly about RPing conspiracies of any kind. It focus a little on Big Level conspiracies, Technocracy-style, but it is useful for any good game with cults and conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}